      {
         "id": "SECTION_game",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Game\n\nThis game turns the practices of **Measuring in three dimensions** (<htcite0>) into three levels. Each level has two exercises:\n\n1. **One direction (1D):** measure the blue string with the ruler, then measure the side of a polygon that rests on the ruler.\n2. **Two directions (2D):** read the two rulers of a square, then the two rulers of a rectangle, and choose the correct pair of measures.\n3. **Three directions (3D):** read the three rulers of a cube, then the three rulers of another solid with different dimensions, and choose the correct triple of measures.\n\nChoose the answer that matches the rulers. A wrong answer stays marked, so you can try again, and the explanation appears when you find the correct measure. The rule is always the same: start at **0**, keep the object straight along the ruler and read the mark where it ends.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "b56ef907-93eb-45ee-ae22-ce4f364ffa4e",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Measuring in three dimensions",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"htMeasureGame\" id=\"htMeasureGame\"><div class=\"htMeasureHeader\"><span class=\"htMeasureLevel\" id=\"htMeasureLevel\"></span><span class=\"htMeasureQuestion\" id=\"htMeasureQuestion\"></span><span class=\"htMeasureScore\" id=\"htMeasureScore\"></span></div><div class=\"htMeasurePrompt\" id=\"htMeasurePrompt\"></div><div class=\"htMeasureCanvas\" id=\"htMeasureCanvas\"></div><div class=\"htMeasureChoices\" id=\"htMeasureChoices\"></div><div class=\"htMeasureFeedback\" id=\"htMeasureFeedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div class=\"htMeasureButtons\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"htMeasureNext\" class=\"htMeasureButton htMeasureHidden\"></button><button type=\"button\" id=\"htMeasureRestart\" class=\"htMeasureButton\"></button></div><div class=\"htMeasureHidden\"><span id=\"htMeasureLevelTemplate\">Level {n} of {total}: {desc}</span><span id=\"htMeasureLevel1\">one ruler, one direction</span><span id=\"htMeasureLevel2\">two rulers, two directions</span><span id=\"htMeasureLevel3\">three rulers, three directions</span><span id=\"htMeasureQuestionTemplate\">Question {q} of {total}</span><span id=\"htMeasureScoreTemplate\">Score: {score} of {total}</span><span id=\"htMeasurePromptString\">What is the length of the blue string?</span><span id=\"htMeasurePromptSide\">The {shape} rests on the ruler. What is the measure of the side that lies on the ruler?</span><span id=\"htMeasurePromptPair\">Which pair of measures do the two rulers show? (length × height)</span><span id=\"htMeasurePromptTriple\">Which triple of measures do the three rulers show? (length × width × height)</span><span id=\"htMeasureShape0\">triangle</span><span id=\"htMeasureShape1\">square</span><span id=\"htMeasureShape2\">pentagon</span><span id=\"htMeasureShape3\">hexagon</span><span id=\"htMeasureFactString\">The string ends at {v} on the ruler, so its length is {v}.</span><span id=\"htMeasureFactSide\">The side of the {shape} that lies on the ruler ends at {v}, so it measures {v}.</span><span id=\"htMeasureFactPair\">The horizontal ruler shows {a} and the vertical ruler shows {b}, so the pair is {a} × {b}.</span><span id=\"htMeasureFactTriple\">The rulers show length {a}, width {b} and height {c}, so the triple is {a} × {b} × {c}.</span><span id=\"htMeasureCorrect\">Correct!</span><span id=\"htMeasureWrong\">Not quite, try again.</span><span id=\"htMeasureHint\">Remember: start at 0, keep the object straight and read the mark where it ends.</span><span id=\"htMeasureLevelComplete\">Level complete!</span><span id=\"htMeasureGameComplete\">Game complete! Congratulations!</span><span id=\"htMeasureWordNext\">Next question</span><span id=\"htMeasureWordNextLevel\">Next level</span><span id=\"htMeasureWordRestart\">Restart</span><span id=\"htMeasureWordPlayAgain\">Play again</span><span id=\"htMeasureWordLength\">Length</span><span id=\"htMeasureWordWidth\">Width</span><span id=\"htMeasureWordHeight\">Height</span></div></div>",
